db_find_or_create_user.s:
New db helper: plain user creation without the rpb class, so a free registration can provision a login account while 'full access' (rpb) stays tied to payment.

File: src/lib/db/index.ts. Insert right after find_or_create_player_user (ends line 405). Copy that function's shape but never touch c/rpb:

  export async function find_or_create_user(email: string, password_hash?: string, phones?: string[]): Promise<string> {
    const existing = await find_user_by_email(email) as (User & { i: string }) | undefined;
    if (existing) {
      const patch: Partial<User> = { e: existing.e, s: 'u' };
      if (phones?.length && !existing.ph?.length) patch.ph = phones;
      await edit_point(existing.i, patch);
      return existing.i;
    }
    const user_id = new_id();
    const u: User = { s: 'u', e: email, d: Date.now() };
    if (password_hash) u.p = password_hash;
    if (phones?.length) u.ph = phones;
    await create(u, undefined, user_id);
    return user_id;
  }

Why: /api/register (next step) must give the registrant a login account + session immediately (no payment), but must NOT grant rpb — rpb means 'TEAMUP enrolled / full access' and is granted only by confirm() after payment (src/lib/confirm.ts:60). find_or_create_player_user can't be reused because it force-adds rpb (src/lib/db/index.ts:389).

Tests (write first, watch them fail for the stated reason): new file src/lib/db/find_or_create_user.test.ts copied from find_or_create_player_user.test.ts (same fake_qdrant vi.mock of $lib/db/get_qdrant + $lib/server/secrets). Replace the describe block with find_or_create_user cases:
1. 'creates an email-only user with no classes': call find_or_create_user('mom@b.co', 'hash', ['2348012345678']); expect u.e === 'mom@b.co', u.c undefined, u.p === 'hash', u.ph deep-equals ['2348012345678'], u.n undefined.
2. 'reuses the same user for a second kid (same email), no duplicate': two calls, same id, one user row.
3. 'does not add rpb to an existing user': pre-seed store.set('u_seed', { s:'u', i:'u_seed', e:'mom@b.co', c:['fab'], d:0 }); call find_or_create_user('mom@b.co'); expect u.c deep-equals ['fab'] (no rpb added).
4. 'backfills phone only when the user has none': pre-seed user without ph; call with ['2348012345678']; expect u.ph set; second call with different phone leaves it unchanged.

