repurpose_register_init_payment.s:
Repurpose POST /api/register-init-payment: it no longer creates registrations. It now inits Paystack for an EXISTING pending registration (the 'unlock full access' step).

Rewrite src/routes/api/register-init-payment/+server.ts entirely (keep the heavy console.log style of the old file - this repo relies on verbose server logs). New body contract: { registrationId }. New logic:

  import { json } from '@sveltejs/kit';
  import type { RequestHandler } from '@sveltejs/kit';
  import { get } from '$lib/db';
  import { paystack_init } from '$lib/paystack';
  import { dev } from '$app/environment';
  import { DEV_REG_FEE, REG_AMOUNT } from '$lib/constants';
  import type { Registration } from '$lib/types/registration';

  const base_kobo = () => (dev ? DEV_REG_FEE : REG_AMOUNT * 100);

  export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, url, locals }) => {
    const data = await request.json();
    const id = data.registrationId;
    if (!id) return json({ error: 'Missing registrationId' }, { status: 400 });
    const reg = await get<Registration>(id);
    if (!reg) return json({ error: 'Registration not found' }, { status: 404 });
    const owner = locals?.user?.email;
    if (!owner || reg.e !== owner) return json({ error: 'Not your registration' }, { status: 403 });
    if (reg.st === 'i') return json({ error: 'Already unlocked' }, { status: 400 });

    const p_name = `${reg.fn || ''} ${reg.ln || ''}`.trim();
    const phone = locals?.user?.ph?.[0] ? String(locals.user.ph[0]) : '';
    const result = await paystack_init(reg.e, reg.amt, reg.i as string, p_name, `${url.origin}/payment/callback`, { a: 'beee', regId: reg.i, phone });

    return json({
      success: true,
      authorization_url: result.authorization_url,
      access_code: result.access_code,
      reference: result.reference,
      registrationId: reg.i,
      amount: reg.amt,
      discounted: reg.amt < base_kobo()
    });
  };

Why reference = reg id: paystack_init (src/lib/paystack.ts:128) already uses registration_id as the Paystack transaction reference, and confirm() (src/lib/confirm.ts:26) looks the reg up by that same reference. So the existing /payment/callback + /api/verify-payment + webhook path works untouched for the unlock flow.

Rewrite src/routes/api/register-init-payment/register-init-payment.test.ts: keep the $app/environment + $lib/paystack mocks; replace the $lib/db mock with one exposing get() over a seeded store Map plus new_id/search_by_payload/create unused stubs. mock_handler(body, locals?) with { request, url, locals }. Cases:
1. missing registrationId -> 400 'Missing registrationId'.
2. unknown id -> 404 'Registration not found'.
3. reg owned by someone else (reg.e !== locals.user.email) -> 403 'Not your registration'.
4. no session -> 403.
5. already paid reg (st 'i') -> 400 'Already unlocked'.
6. pending reg, discounted amt 1_350_000: success true, amount 1_350_000, discounted true, access_code + authorization_url present, paystack_init called with (email, 1350000, regId, 'John Doe', callback url ending /payment/callback, metadata containing phone from session ph).
7. pending reg, full amt 1_500_000: amount 1_500_000, discounted false.
8. dev mode + reg amt = DEV_REG_FEE: discounted false (amt === base).

Implement, run `pnpm vitest run src/routes/api/register-init-payment/register-init-payment.test.ts` green, then full gate `pnpm test && pnpm check`. Commit scoped to this step.

dashboard_unlock.s:
Dashboard 'unlock full access' button: for a pending registration, the button runs the exact same Paystack flow the register page used to run.

File: src/routes/dashboard/+page.svelte.

1. Script: add state after line 11: let is_paying = $state(false); let pay_error = $state('');
Add function after become_partner (after line 51):

  async function unlock_full_access() {
    if (!active_reg?.i) return;
    is_paying = true;
    pay_error = '';
    let auth_url = '';
    try {
      const r = await fetch('/api/register-init-payment', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ registrationId: active_reg.i })
      });
      if (!r.ok) {
        const e = await r.json().catch(() => ({}));
        throw new Error(e.error || 'Payment initialization failed');
      }
      const d = await r.json();
      if (!d.access_code) throw new Error('Invalid response from payment gateway');
      auth_url = d.authorization_url;
      const PaystackPop = (await import('@paystack/inline-js')).default;
      const popup = new PaystackPop();
      const fb = setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = auth_url; }, 15000);
      popup.resumeTransaction(d.access_code, {
        onLoad: () => clearTimeout(fb),
        onSuccess: (tx) => { clearTimeout(fb); window.location.href = `/payment/callback?reference=${tx.reference}`; },
        onCancel: () => { clearTimeout(fb); is_paying = false; },
        onError: () => { clearTimeout(fb); window.location.href = auth_url; }
      });
    } catch (error) {
      if (auth_url) window.location.href = auth_url;
      else { pay_error = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error'; is_paying = false; }
    }
  }

2. Status label (line 91): `{active_reg.st === 'i' ? 'Paid' : 'Pending'}` -> `{active_reg.st === 'i' ? 'Full access' : 'Registered'}`. ('Pending' is now wrong - registration completes free.)
3. Unlock box: inside .reg-detail, right after the closing </dl> (line 93), before the div closes:

  {#if active_reg?.st === 'r'}
    <div class="unlock-box">
      <p class="unlock-text">Your player is registered. Full access to the complete championship experience unlocks with the one-time fee.</p>
      <button class="dash-btn" onclick={unlock_full_access} disabled={is_paying}>{is_paying ? 'Opening payment…' : 'unlock full access'}</button>
      {#if pay_error}<p class="unlock-error" role="alert">{pay_error}</p>{/if}
    </div>
  {/if}

4. Styles in the <style> block (reuse tokens): .unlock-box { margin-top: 18px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; } .unlock-text { font-family: var(--font-registration); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; } .unlock-error { font-family: var(--font-registration); font-size: 13px; color: var(--error); margin: 0; }

